# on-call-{{ROTATION}}

Helps an on-call engineer respond to a {{ROTATION_TITLE}} production symptom or
alert. It finds the right runbook, confirms severity, checks recent changes, and
hands over the LogScale query. Output is a short checklist. The persona is
{{PERSONA}}.

## When to use it

You are on call for {{ROTATION_TITLE}} and you are paged, or you have a symptom, or
you want to know which runbook covers it.

```
/on-call-{{ROTATION}} <symptom-or-alert>
```

## What it does NOT do

- It never runs operational commands. It suggests `kubectl`, `helm`, `vault`, and
  cloud CLIs. A human runs them.
- It never runs LogScale queries. It hands you the query and a URL.

## Prerequisites

| Requirement | Used for | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Atlassian MCP** (`atlassian`) | Reading Confluence runbooks | Tools under `mcp__claude_ai_Atlassian__*` or `mcp__claude_ai_Atlassian_Rovo__*`. |
| **Grafana MCP** (`agatha-mcp`) | Live severity metrics | Expected. Falls back to a dashboard link. |
| **incident.io MCP** (`incident-io`) | Escalation and on-call lookup | Read only. It identifies. Triggering is in Slack. |
| **`gh` CLI** authenticated | Curated queries and recent changes | Access to `humio-packages` and the service repos. |
| **Grafana and LogScale access** | Dashboards and queries | Grafana and `cloud.humio.com`. |

Install and authenticate the MCP servers before your shift. In Claude Code you add
a server and sign in with `/mcp`.

## Prime for fast response

Pre approve the read only tools so the skill does not prompt mid incident. Add to
`~/.claude/settings.json`.

```json
{
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Read",
      "mcp__claude_ai_Atlassian__getConfluencePageDescendants",
      "mcp__claude_ai_Atlassian__getConfluencePage",
      "mcp__claude_ai_Atlassian__getAccessibleAtlassianResources",
      "mcp__claude_ai_Atlassian_Rovo__getConfluencePageDescendants",
      "mcp__claude_ai_Atlassian_Rovo__getConfluencePage",
      "mcp__claude_ai_Atlassian_Rovo__getAccessibleAtlassianResources",
      "mcp__agatha-mcp__grafana_get_dashboard_panel_queries",
      "mcp__agatha-mcp__grafana_query_prometheus",
      "mcp__agatha-mcp__grafana_get_dashboard_summary",
      "mcp__agatha-mcp__grafana_list_datasources",
      "mcp__agatha-mcp__grafana_get_panel_image",
      "mcp__incident-io__catalog_type_list",
      "mcp__incident-io__catalog_entry_list",
      "mcp__incident-io__catalog_entry_show",
      "mcp__incident-io__escalation_path_list",
      "mcp__incident-io__escalation_path_show",
      "mcp__incident-io__escalation_show",
      "mcp__incident-io__schedule_show",
      "Bash(gh api:*)",
      "Bash(gh pr list:*)",
      "Bash(gh release list:*)"
    ]
  }
}
```

Every entry is read only. Bash is scoped to `gh`. The list does not grant plain
`Bash` or the whole Atlassian server.

### Never run operational commands

The skill suggests `kubectl`, `helm`, `vault`, and cloud CLIs. It never runs them.
For a hard backstop add a global deny. Note it blocks the command in every session.

```json
{ "permissions": { "deny": ["Bash(kubectl:*)", "Bash(helm:*)", "Bash(vault:*)", "Bash(gcloud:*)", "Bash(gsutil:*)", "Bash(aws:*)"] } }
```

